; Collected flags of the hearts, parchments, the red scroll and the crosses ($8525-$8540)
;
; One byte for each pick-up item of the room item table #R$8EDF (the pointer in the item's record is the address of
; its flag). 0 means the item is still there, $FF (ITEM_GONE) that it has been taken: the item spawner #R$8957 (via
; #R$896B) does not create an item whose flag is $FF, so a taken item stays gone. The flags are zeroed by #R$85FC at
; the start of a game; the flag of an item taken in a room survives leaving and re-entering the room. Each flag is
; named after its item and the room it is in; the comment gives the item's row and column in the room.
;
; +$00-$08: hearts (item type 0, #R$A70B): one more life, up to 9 (the status bar shows them, #R$854C).
; +$09-$0E: parchments (type 5, #R$A836): taking one shows the parchment text (#R$850E).
; +$0F: the red scroll of Satan's room (type 6, #R$A668), only present after the chalice.
; +$10-$1B: the twelve crosses (types 1 and 2, #R$A782/#R$A777, counted in #R$854D). The eight crosses of type 1
; (CrossRoomN) can be taken while the wheel of faith #R$851E is at rest, the four of type 2 (WheelCrossRoomN) only
; after it has been turned.
@label=HeartRoom2
g$8525 DEFB $00 ; room 2, row 7, column 12, item type 0
@label=HeartRoom10
 $8526 DEFB $00 ; room 10, row 18, column 10, item type 0
@label=HeartRoom11
 $8527 DEFB $00 ; room 11, row 4, column 2, item type 0
@label=HeartRoom12
 $8528 DEFB $00 ; room 12, row 6, column 16, item type 0
@label=HeartRoom15
